					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/catboy637" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1322622); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1322622&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973866" alt="catboy637" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1322622)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/catboy637" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1322622); return false;" >catboy637</a></span> <span class="odate time_1342144854 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Jul 2012 02:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1506711">
									

<p>Diseases wouldn't transfer 1:1 though, not just alien disease which infects humans. After a while, whether a few weeks or a couple years, the disease would adjust and adapt to humans. Just as diseases in cows adapted to humans once humans started breeding and living with cows, alien diseases would (eventually) adapt and adjust to humans once aliens start living near humans. Even if they don't like near humans, war is a quick way to spread disease (see WWI). Perhaps not as unsanitary, but any close contact with corpses, weapons and debris could spread illness.</p>

							</div>

								
					
