					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1019930&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973866" alt="Anaxagoras" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1019930)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;" >Anaxagoras</a></span> <span class="odate time_1342145156 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Jul 2012 02:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1506717">
									

<p>If the aliens have a different biochemistry, diseases won't spread. Evolution doesn't work that way. Moreover, war with aliens would probably involve very little direct interspecies contact.</p>
<p>Our atmosphere likely wouldn't be poisonous. The only gas to really watch out for would be oxygen, and oxygen is useful enough across multiple possible multicellular biochemistries that there's a good chance aliens would need it too. Nitrogen, the only other gas present in really large quantities is harmless to basically everything ever. Nitrogen doesn't do <em>shit</em>.</p>

							</div>

								
					
