					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hornby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1259135); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1259135&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973866" alt="Hornby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1259135)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hornby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1259135); return false;" >Hornby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1342145479 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Jul 2012 02:11</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1506720">
									

<p>And, to boot, if Earth's atmosphere was so unfriendly to aliens that they'd only be able to survive in artificially created atmospheres in suits and airtight containers, there are plenty of other planets with different (or no) atmospheres to go and colonize/conquer/whatever. In the grand cost of interstellar expansion, it's just simply not worth the resources to try and invade a planet where you can't survive - either leave well enough alone, or drop an asteroid on the planet to wipe out the inhabitants if you don't want neighbors, but don't try and conquer/colonize/whatever.</p>

							</div>

								
					
