<blockquote>
<p>… Isn't this basically what Stephen Hawking said a year or two ago, only more verbose?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yup.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, people automatically assume that &quot;Europeans had guns, therefore automatic win!&quot; when that typically only applied in cases of large Native American charges at fixed positions</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This whole paragraph is true, which is why I said exactly what it says in the actual piece. And I quote:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>While technology was a major boon to the European conquest of the New World, the largest killer of Native Americans was European disease.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As for the rest, that's the entire idea. This isn't a pessimistic paper, it's about how humanity can fight the aliens and survive. Not &quot;well, we're doomed&quot;. More like, &quot;we will be doomed if we don't know what we're doing&quot;.</p>

