<p>Hm&#8230; Kinda odd, i got a lot more gloom and doom feeling with a thin sliver of hope, rather than a &quot;Here's what to do and we're okay.&quot;</p>
<p>Also, yes, you did say how the tech wasn't the only advantage, that was a semi-hunger-driven tangent on so, SO, many things I've seen around the internet lately basically going &quot;If the Native American tribes had guns they'd still be controlling the continent!&quot; They had guns. They had a <em>shit load</em> of guns. They bought, salvaged or stole them from the Europeans. Most groups that stayed away were because it was either too loud to use when hunting, or because they didn't have reasonable infrastructure and constant trade to keep them supplied and functional, rather than any sort of honor or like that. But, &quot;Cowboys use guns always and Indians use bows and arrows always&quot; is a trope so, people think that's how it was. Same gripe with the film of The Last Samurai, aside from it being another &quot;Tom Cruise needs his ego fluffed&quot; picture.</p>
<p>Wow I'm getting angry again&#8230; I needs me a snack. *consumes chocolate drizzled waffle-bites*</p>

