					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1204404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973867" alt="wishun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1204404)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;" >wishun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1342465692 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Jul 2012 19:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1509721">
									

<p>Two unwarranted assumptions in here.<br />
First, as already mentioned, there is no reason to assume biological compatibility. Even if they are biochemically similar enough to be interested in Earth as a place to live, it does not neccessarily follow that they will be tasty to Earth infections. For example, what if the invaders are robots? There are an uncountable number of other plausible scenarios where infection is a non-issue for either side.</p>
<p>Second, why does everyone always assume that the aliens will be more technologically advanced in every field? Yes, if they come to us then they have at least one technology that we lack. But that could be the <em>only</em> advanced tech they have. Maybe they discovered one weird trick that let's them make worm-holes with vacumn tubes, or Babbage difference engines. To keep it related to this article, maybe they have advanced physics but medical experiments are forbidden by the dominant religion so they are still using the equivalent of leeches. What I am trying to say is that FTL =/= laser rifles, energy shields, anti-gravity, or any other cool sci-fi tech.</p>

							</div>

								
					
