														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1561156">
									

<p>Love the &quot;learning from history&quot; aspect, hate the short-sighted assumptions about aliens having to be thousands of years ahead of us to develop practical FTL.</p>
<p>We are arguably just a few dozen years from practical FTL <span style="text-decoration: underline;">today</span>, why the assumptions that aliens will have more than 50 years on us, just because they have FTL?</p>
<p>(Which is not to say that having 50 years on us isn't incredible - most countries today could probably defeat the entire world if transported fifty years back. Even then we're not counting that most theoretical forms of FTL can also double as devastating weapons.)</p>

