<p>(FTL isn't necessarily impossible, but it isn't effective with a slow acceleration rate)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm pretty sure general relativity says that FTL <em>is</em> necessarily impossible under all conditions, full stop, no asterisk. General relativity probably won't be the last word in physics or anything, granted, but I wouldn't take a bet on us so much as <em>witnessing</em> anything exceeding c in my lifetime, much less us learning how to make it happen in a controlled and useful fashion.</p>

