			<div class="content" id="post-content-1561275">
									

<p>The solid-core NTR still has travel times in the order of three months or so, compared to about eight months with the best chemical-rocket designs. The maximum speed (dV) a realistic NTR could accelerate you to (given that you're already in space) is around 10km/s, without any gravitational trickery (which you would use). The Space Shuttle orbiter could reach 300m/s, for comparison.</p>

