    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-1884841">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-1884841">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,1884841)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-1884841">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/devilot" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(299577); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=299577&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973867" alt="Devilot" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=299577)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/devilot" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(299577); return false;" >Devilot</a></span> <span class="odate time_1383574181 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Nov 2013 14:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1884841">
									

<p>This is an interesting article, but it makes some problematic assumptions. It assumes that aliens will be psychologically similar to humanity, which is not a given&#8230; and even its assumption of more advanced technology is not a given. Science fiction has presented potential methods by which this may not be the case, of varying plausibility. Perhaps they have to travel via generation ship or similar, and some disaster on the way set back their technological progress. Perhaps they developed the ability to build spaceships instinctively, the same way bees know to build hives. Perhaps there's a really simple trick to practical FTL travel that we haven't discovered yet, but some alien race that still considers steel armor and arquebuses the height of military technology has. Maybe they inherited their technology from another civilization and have difficulty understanding how it works or generalizing it, leading them to be advanced in only certain areas. Maybe they're more technologically advanced in certain areas but more comparable to us &#8212; or even behind us &#8212; in others due to aspects of their culture or psychology that blinded them to progress in those areas.</p>
<p>Really, we can't make many assumptions when dealing with extraterrestrial intelligences.</p>

							</div>

								
					
